{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Place</b> — Rabbi Moses said: שִׁמְרָה is like שְׁמִירָה, on the pattern of עֲצָמָה, יִרְבֶּה. In my opinion: the verb is defective, like שִׁיתָה י׳ מַחְסוֹם, or כְּדָמוּת מַחְסוֹם." "<b>And the word</b> שָׁמְרָה — like: שָׁמְרָה נַפְשִׁי וְהַצִּילֵנִי (Psalm 25:20)." "<b>And the word</b> נְצֹרָה — is imperative, and the dagesh is added in the tzadi, for elegance of expression, like: אִם־יִקְרְךָ עָו‍ֹן (Proverbs 24:16), and likewise the tzadi in נְצֹרָה, כִּי־הִיא חַיֶּיךָ (Proverbs 4:13)." "<b>And the word</b> דֶּל — like דֶּלֶת (door), for the tav is a feminine sign, הַדֶּלֶת תָּסוּב עַל־צִירָה (the door turns on its hinge), and behold the meaning is like: פִּתְחִי פִּיִךְ (open your mouth), and the meaning is that He help him not to speak with his tongue what is not proper."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 141, :notes {0 "Resolved ה׳ to HaShem per voice rules. The three Hebrew examples after 'like' are cited as forms whose vowel pattern שִׁמְרָה parallels; יִרְבֶּה appears to be a prooftext whose connection to the pattern argument is terse and left as-is."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:33.801634487Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}